own tuple/tag. Copy the whole input before parsing; store only Engine sealed records/private arrays.\",\"envelope\":[\"revisions[5]\",\"registrySha256\",\"id\",\"after[]\",\"localTypes[]\",\"fields[]\",\"attributes[]\",\"rows[]\",\"maxima\",\"body[]\"],\"caps\":{\"encodedBytes\":1048576,\"nodes\":32768,\"locals\":1024,\"depth\":64,\"fields\":1024,\"attributes\":256,\"rows\":256,\"dependencies\":256,\"idBytes\":128,\"constantLoop\":1024,\"listCapacity\":65536,\"workUnits\":2147483647,\"scratchBytes\":16777216},\"types\":{\"bool\":1,\"i32\":2,\"u32\":3,\"i64\":4,\"u64\":5,\"entity\":6,\"handle\":7,\"result\":8,\"resultKind\":9,\"resultOutcome\":10,\"effectError\":11,\"current\":12,\"rowClaim\":13},\"statements\":{\"let\":1,\"assign\":2,\"if\":3,\"for\":4,\"return\":5,\"require\":6,\"write\":7,\"setAt\":8,\"claim\":9},\"expressions\":{\"constant\":1,\"local\":2,\"tick\":3,\"worldEntity\":4,\"resultCount\":5,\"resultAt\":6,\"project\":7,\"unary\":8,\"binary\":9,\"convert\":10,\"has\":11,\"read\":12,\"count\":13,\"at\":14,\"current\":15,\"hookInput\":16},\"statementShapes\":{\"let\":[\"local\",\"expr\"],\"assign\":[\"local\",\"expr\"],\"if\":[\"condition\",\"then[]\",\"else[]\"],\"for\":[\"readonlyI32Local\",\"bound\",\"body[]\"],\"return\":[],\"require\":[\"condition\",\"fault\"],\"write\":[\"entity\",\"field\",\"value\"],\"setAt\":[\"claim\",\"field\",\"value\"],\"claim\":[\"local\",\"result\",\"row\",\"owner\",\"index\"]},\"expressionShapes\":{\"constant\":[\"type\",\"value\"],\"local\":[\"local\"],\"tick\":[],\"worldEntity\":[],\"resultCount\":[],\"resultAt\":[\"index\"],\"project\":[\"value\",\"member\"],\"unary\":[\"operator\",\"checked\",\"value\"],\"binary\":[\"operator\",\"checked\",\"left\",\"right\"],\"convert\":[\"type\",\"checked\",\"value\"],\"has\":[\"entity\",\"field\"],\"read\":[\"entity\",\"field\"],\"count\":[\"entity\",\"field\"],\"at\":[\"entity\",\"field\",\"index\"],\"current\":[\"entity\",\"attribute\"],\"hookInput\":[\"member\"]},\"bounds\":{\"constant\":1,\"results\":2,\"listCount\":3},\"boundShapes\":{\"constant\":[\"i32\"],\"results\":[],\"listCount\":[\"stableOwnerLocal\",\"field\"]},\"unary\":[\"negate\",\"not\",\"complement\"],\"binary\":[\"add\",\"subtract\",\"multiply\",\"divide\",\"remainder\",\"equal\",\"notEqual\",\"less\",\"lessEqual\",\"greater\",\"greaterEqual\",\"and\",\"or\",\"xor\",\"shiftLeft\",\"shiftRight\"],\"arithmetic\":\"Exact same-type i32/u32/i64/u64 operands and result; shifts take i32 right operand and mask 31/63. Comparisons produce bool. Boolean operators accept bool only. Identity/handle and closed enums permit exact-type equality only; compare every identity part. No identity arithmetic or conversions. Numeric conversions explicitly select checked/unchecked C# semantics. Negate accepts signed integers, not accepts bool, complement accepts integers. Signed min/-1 division faults even unchecked; remainder follows C#. No string/object/box path.\",\"projections\":{\"result\":[\"handle\",\"typeId\",\"target\",\"source\",\"appliedTick\",\"tick\",\"kind\",\"outcome\",\"crossedZero\",\"error\",\"ordinal\",\"hasDueTick\",\"dueTick\"],\"handle\":[\"worldId\",\"instanceId\",\"generation\",\"isDefault\"],\"current\":[\"present\",\"value\"]},\"current\":\"Noncreating Engine ledger read returns (present,i64). Missing/foreign/dead entity, component or registered ledger gives absent; value is valid only in the present branch. No mutable ledger/Attribute access.\",\"faults\":[\"effect_access_violation\",\"effect_budget_invariant\"],\"validation\":\"Exact revisions, tuple arities/tags/types, canonical values, lexical scope, definite assignment, immutable loop indices, return branches, present-dominated Current.value, declared field/attribute/row indexes, unique declarations, acyclic dependencies and hooks; reject before Ready. Helpers inline with fresh locals. For captures bound once and owns increment. Stable Count owner cannot change in loop. Reject shared/cyclic in-memory nodes during construction; serialized tree contains no references. Current presence proofs merge by intersection of continuing branches; returning branches do not flow to successors. A loop invalidates all proofs of outer current locals assigned anywhere in its body before checking any iteration, and after the loop; the body may establish fresh present proofs after assignment. Branch-local declarations never escape.\",\"work\":\"checked-u64 sequence sum; if charges condition+1+max(branch); for charges bound+1+N*(2+body); return/require/let/assign each 1 plus expressions. Every expression is 1 plus children. Storage read/write adds actual fixed width in bytes; list overwrite adds capacity*valueWidth for normal dirty/snapshot copy plus 1 for reference-indexed dirty lookup. Include all transitive hooks and row checks. No unbounded dirty ledger scan is permitted in F. Startup requires computed work <= declared maxWorkUnits <= cap, batch quota >= sum maxima. Debit actual work before each operation; exhaustion faults.\",\"scratch\":\"Bounded logical interpreter payload slots, not exact CLR/native heap or object sizes. Reserve localBytes*locals + claimBytes*count(rowClaim locals) + claimColumnBytes*sum(maxColumns(local)) + fieldCounterBytes*declaredFields + frameBytes*maximum structural depth + maximum simultaneously active hook scratch. Derive maxColumns(local) from validated Claim syntax and actual row schemas at all statically permitted sites assigning that local; take the maximum per local, then sum all locals independently. Unused claim locals retain the fixed header with zero columns; unrelated schemas add nothing. Branch alternatives retain all declared allocations. Claims cannot be assigned/replaced or returned; loop reuse occurs only after previous lexical claim retirement. Each hook recursively reserves its own locals, all declared field counters, structural frames and nested active scratch. Root declared fields must include hook-expanded coverage. Use checked u64 arithmetic and reject derived or declared scratch above scratchBytes cap before Ready; caller estimates never establish column counts.\",\"maxima\":[\"maxWrites\",\"maxIndexedWrites\",\"maxWriteBytes\",\"maxWorkUnits\",\"maxScratchBytes\"],\"hooks\":\"Registry-owned immutable fragments with owner/old/new/reason inputs and exact revisions; cannot be supplied or suppressed by reducer. Reject unknown or cyclic hook closures; expand write/field/work bounds. Scalar write validates/charges, tracks value, suppresses dirty/hooks on equality, otherwise stores then appends ordinary Dirty/PendingHooks. Drain only newly appended suffix: remove entry then Changing then Changed, both observe stored value; nested writes drain recursively; Changed does not run after Changing fault. Preserve partial writes and original operation exception.\",\"lifecycle\":\"Generated registration supplies data outside F; old executable registration rejects before construction. Freeze dependency order (ordinal ASCII ID tie break), all metadata and exact bindings before Ready. Per-invocation lease expires independently, result storage survives full reducer round; once even empty authority Tick; no confirmed/predicted invocation.\",\"scratchLayout\":{\"localBytes\":128,\"claimBytes\":256,\"frameBytes\":32,\"claimColumnBytes\":32,\"fieldCounterBytes\":8},\"hookSchema\":{\"version\":1,\"envelope\":[\"version\",\"ownerLayout\",\"ownerSlot\",\"ownerOrdinal\",\"valueCodec\",\"localTypes[]\",\"fields[]\",\"maxima\",\"changing[]\",\"changed[]\"],\"fieldShape\":[\"registryFieldIndex\",\"access\",\"maxWrites\"],\"fingerprint\":\"lowercase SHA256 of canonical UTF8 JSON envelope bytes (no length prefix). References use frozen registry field indices; the envelope contains no claimed validated/acyclic/metric flag. Registry descriptors bind the fingerprint to the exact owner location and codec; do not hash a copy of descriptors back into the fragment.\",\"inputs\":{\"owner\":\"entity\",\"old\":\"valueCodec\",\"new\":\"valueCodec\",\"reason\":\"i32\"},\"reason\":\"Local=2 at this seam. The fragment cannot choose a reason or owner. Old/new are copied values; storage is already written when Changing starts.\",\"restrictions\":\"Same expression and statement grammar with hookInput enabled. Claim, SetAt, rowClaim locals and result/ResultAt/ResultCount are unsupported inside hooks; indexed destinations cannot have hooks. Hooks may read declared scalar/list values and write declared ordinary scalars; scalar-write hooks recursively expand. Caller cannot override or skip Changing/Changed.\",\"validation\":\"Validate both bodies, exact input/property/type domains, field permissions and per-field bounds. Derive metrics from operations, never trust summaries. Changing executes before Changed; a fault suppresses Changed. Reject any reachable write cycle among concrete field bindings. Propagate every transitive field, write, indexed (always zero for hook writes), byte, work and active-scratch cost into each caller. Read-only access to the owner field does not create a hook dependency.\",\"maxima\":[\"maxWrites\",\"maxIndexedWrites\",\"maxWriteBytes\",\"maxWorkUnits\",\"maxScratchBytes\"]},\"rowSchema\":{\"version\":1,\"envelope\":[\"version\",\"id\",\"ownerLayout\",\"indexed\",\"capacity\",\"columns[]\",\"stateColumn\",\"pendingValue\",\"readyColumn\",\"keys[]\"],\"columnShape\":[\"registryFieldIndex\",\"role\",\"maxReducerWrites\"],\"roles\":[\"captured\",\"output\",\"ready\",\"status\"],\"keyShape\":[\"columnIndex\",\"selector\"],\"rules\":\"At least one status column and one bool ready column. stateColumn is a status column; pendingValue is a canonical typed constant matching its codec. indexed=true requires all columns be hook-free lists of identical positive capacity; indexed=false requires scalars and capacity=1, index=0. All column bindings use the same concrete owner layout; duplicate columns/key selectors reject. captured/output/ready columns have maxReducerWrites=0. Status columns have a positive i32 maximum. readyColumn has role ready and bool codec. Keys must use captured columns and include all six required HandleWorld/HandleInstance/HandleGeneration/TypeId/Target/Source selectors with exact codecs; any extra payload selectors require matching captured payload schema in the bound fact plan.\",\"claim\":\"The result is copied from the current batch, not an authored constant. Require exact full six-part association and current row state equal pendingValue. Applied requires ready=true and a captured Tick binding equal result.Tick; Rejected requires ready=false. Other result kinds/outcomes reject. The claim retains full record/storage identities, owner/index/extent, immutable key values and invocation identity. Each SetAt rechecks them and the row status declaration; replacing or moving rows invalidates it. A status write may change state from pending, so subsequent writes under the same claim check its captured initial state plus Engine-recorded own status mutations, never accept external reassignment.\",\"work\":\"Preflight and every claim recheck charge 1 per column binding/extent check plus codec width per key read, 6 full-identity comparisons at their codec widths, 1 ready check and ready width; derived from concrete schema, no caller preflightWork. SetAt additionally charges actual list-copy and reference-indexed dirty costs.\"},\"scratchStorage\":{\"claimColumnLayout\":[[\"EngineStorageReference\",8],[\"FixedScalarValue\",16],[\"AttemptedWriteCount\",8]],\"fieldCounterLayout\":[[\"AttemptedWriteCount\",8]],\"allocation\":\"Validated syntax, row/field descriptors, binding indices, permissions, codec tags and derived per-local maxima are immutable startup storage bounded by encoded source/registry caps; share them, never duplicate metadata per claim or request. Allocate dense local, field-counter, claim-column and control-frame arrays from derived maxima outside F and reuse them. No per-write allocation, unbounded map, boxed scalar, dynamic closure or hidden per-column array in a fixed header. FixedScalarValue uses two u64 slots for every one of the six codecs, including entity; codec comes from frozen schema. Claim header256 and local128 are logical payload budgets. Allocate request certificate bytes, association headers and storage-reference slices before F; captured/output scalars use canonical slices and retained admitted snapshot rather than duplicate variable scalar arrays.\",\"implementationBoundary\":\"Logical slots and canonical encoded-byte quotas are not exact managed allocations. Runtime must separately bound and disclose allocator object/array framing, alignment, pool bookkeeping and execution stack using validated caps and slot/array counts. Frame32 is a logical control-frame charge; use a bounded preallocated explicit stack or separately prove a bounded native/CLR stack implementation from structural and acyclic hook limits. Moving allocation outside F does not remove its reservation. JS oracle Maps, JSON strings and object copies model validation/identity, not a production allocator or proof of allocation-free execution.\"}},\"registryBinding\":{\"version\":1,\"fieldShape\":[\"componentKey\",\"fieldKey\",\"layout\",\"slot\",\"ordinal\",\"category\",\"codec\",\"capacity\",\"scope\",\"authority\",\"notify\",\"hookFingerprint\",\"access\",\"maxWrites\"],\"identity\":\"registrySha256 + concrete layout + zero-based component slot + zero-based field ordinal; expand each component occurrence across templates; zero slot and ordinal valid; schema dedup excludes owner and element index\",\"keys\":\"Successor componentId/fieldId remain stable positive descriptor references, never positional IDs. Explicit generated mapping resolves reference keys to every actual concrete descriptor. Reject absent/duplicate/stale/contradictory mappings and right-name/wrong-key. Do not change successor authentication/epoch/retention.\",\"capture\":\"Exact Engine Sync<T> shared ScalarStorage and sealed SyncList<T> only. Bound/attachment installs per-record Engine storage table before entity becomes readable; rebind/reset retires prior handles. Candidates from metadata/accessor/registry code are resolved and checked outside F then discarded; no authored object or callable adapter survives. Full owner/record generation, actual storage identity, category/codec/scope/authority/notify/capacity and hook fragment must match. Consumer registry metadata has the explicit caps recorded here; each canonical hook/fact/row record is validated before use. Program attribute and row entries are integer indices into those captured records. Only rows backed by a validated matching instant fact plan can be claimed. Unknown or duplicate records reject. The oracle trust boundary is the raw Engine-generated physical field and ledger descriptor set and owning Effect declaration, not reducer-authored metadata. Independently validate every record before any program: closed scope(room/aoi/owner/claim/none), authority(server/owner), notify(remote/all), codec/category/capacity, positive stable keys, concrete slot/ordinal ownership, duplicate physical or logical bindings, all attributes/ledgers, all rows/facts and every hook body including unused hooks. Validate the owning payload declaration version, TypeId, lifetime and unique typed fields and recompute its canonical fingerprint; instant/validated flags alone are never evidence. Oracle payload declaration tuples [1,typeId,lifetime,payloadFields] model that independently checked owning declaration; these oracle records do not add Runtime registration or operation-plan opcodes.\",\"borrowing\":\"Has returns false for missing/foreign/dead/component-absent entity; bad descriptor/lease faults. Read/At return copied fixed scalars; Count reads fixed bounded extent. No World/component/container/ref/enumerator escapes. Revalidate live record and storage at each access.\",\"indexed\":\"SetAt only existing element at 0<=index<Count in a claimed aligned row. Count/shape/key/full handle and source/target immutable association revalidated before each mutation. No append/remove/clear/rebind/resize. Indexed/fact destinations must have no authored Changing/Changed/ItemChanged. Preserve normal container dirty/snapshot/projection semantics including equal-element behavior.\",\"access\":{\"read\":0,\"readWrite\":1},\"fieldPermissions\":\"access/maxWrites belong to the plan declaration, not physical identity. read requires maxWrites=0; readWrite requires positive bounded i32. All attempted writes including equal and transitive hook writes count against the declaring field slice. Physical binding tuple is the first twelve members. A field used as captured/output/ready in any row is never F-writable, including via scalar Write or hooks. Indexed F writes require a live claim and that row schema status role.\",\"attributeShape\":[\"layout\",\"componentSlot\",\"attributeId\",\"currentOrdinal\",\"codec\"],\"attributes\":\"Frozen concrete AttributeComponent ledger mapping. layout/componentSlot/currentOrdinal are nonnegative positions verified outside F against actual Engine ledgers; attributeId is nonempty ASCII <=128 bytes and unique within layout; codec is i64. Absent ledger gives absent without creation. Program attributes select registry attribute record indices, not dynamic strings.\",\"caps\":{\"encodedBytes\":16777216,\"layouts\":1024,\"slotsPerLayout\":256,\"fields\":65536,\"attributes\":4096,\"hooks\":1024,\"rows\":256,\"facts\":256}},\"writeAccounting\":{\"scalarFixedBytes\":28,\"indexedFixedBytes\":32,\"scalarLayout\":[[\"owner\",\"entity\"],[\"slot\",\"u32\"],[\"ordinal\",\"u32\"],[\"length\",\"u32\"],[\"value\",\"bytes\"]],\"indexedLayout\":[[\"owner\",\"entity\"],[\"slot\",\"u32\"],[\"ordinal\",\"u32\"],[\"length\",\"u32\"],[\"index\",\"u32\"],[\"value\",\"bytes\"]],\"widths\":{\"bool\":1,\"i32\":4,\"u32\":4,\"i64\":8,\"u64\":8,\"entity\":16},\"debit\":\"Per-field/per-row, invocation and World batch credits debit before mutation including equ