ast; missing/duplicate completion or real callback exception faults preserving original exception and actual partial state, no false Applied/publication/rollback.\",\"admission\":\"Atomically reserve full M/I/byte fact slice with ordinary request credits; refuse without any row/handle/ordinal/result leak. Caller reserves existing row before admission; refused caller reservation is removed ordinarily. No later resize/reassignment of admitted rows. Rejected slices and unused credits release at completion; durable rows remain for normal business consumer.\",\"capacity\":\"Q=pendingRequests; M/I=max declared total/indexed writes per initial instant request; V=max actual codec width. Separate fact quotas cannot be spent in F; finite/period/control facts unsupported. Registry-expanded distinct fields counted once.\",\"claim\":\"Reducer Claim validates exactly one full Handle plus TypeId/Target/Source association with the copied actual result and all row keys. Applied requires ready fact and true settlement Tick, rejection requires its pending reservation. Arithmetic/attribution are read-only in F; only declared status fields writable. Revalidate on every SetAt; expired/cross-context claim faults.\",\"retention\":\"Game retains existing row and immutable attribution until ordinary next-business consumer marks consumed, before reset/destruction/reuse. Source life disappearance does not erase history. Normal ECS checkpoint preserves unconsumed and consumed markers; presentation uses original occurrence Tick. No engine gameplay policy or general result history.\",\"schemaRevision\":1,\"planSchema\":{\"envelope\":[\"version\",\"typeId\",\"payloadFingerprint\",\"payloadFields[]\",\"row\",\"ownerSelector\",\"indexSelector\",\"bindings[]\",\"outputs[]\",\"maxima\"],\"payloadFieldShape\":[\"positiveFieldId\",\"codec\"],\"bindingShape\":[\"columnIndex\",\"selector\"],\"outputShape\":[\"columnIndex\",\"codec\"],\"maxima\":[\"maxWrites\",\"maxIndexedWrites\",\"maxWriteBytes\"],\"selectorShape\":[\"tag\",\"argument\"],\"selectors\":{\"HandleWorld\":[1,\"u64\"],\"HandleInstance\":[2,\"u64\"],\"HandleGeneration\":[3,\"u32\"],\"TypeId\":[4,\"u32\"],\"Target\":[5,\"entity\"],\"Source\":[6,\"entity\"],\"AppliedTick\":[7,\"u64\"],\"Tick\":[8,\"u64\"],\"Payload\":[9,\"declared-payload-codec\"],\"ConstantIndex\":[10,\"i32\"]},\"selectorRules\":\"Non-Payload selectors use argument=0. Payload argument is an existing positive payload field ID. ConstantIndex argument is canonical nonnegative i32 and is legal only as indexSelector. Owner selector must have entity type. Index selector must have i32 type. Payload entries are the exact scalar subset selected from the owning payload descriptor and validated against that fingerprint, never a replacement descriptor; only the six storage codecs are legal in facts.\",\"rules\":\"Exact version/type/fingerprint and row identity; authority instant only. Every captured row column has exactly one Engine binding. Bindings include all six identity selectors and Tick exactly once with exact codec; every row key selector equals its corresponding binding. Every output-role column has exactly one primitive arithmetic output (i32/u32/i64/u64), no output can target captured/ready/status. Every ready column is unique and bool; Engine writes it true last. Status columns are not written by facts. Duplicate/unbound/unknown/wrong-codec fields reject before startup. Derive maxWrites as bindings+outputs+1 ready, indexed as writes when indexed else 0, and maxWriteBytes from actual scalar28/indexed32 plus each codec width; declared maxima must equal these values. Per-column fact maximum is exactly one. Whole-row preflight checks all columns and full budget before Base mutation.\",\"completion\":\"Generated writer receives one ordered primitive tuple matching outputs, checks/debits the complete slice before the first column mutation, supplies immutable binding values, then outputs then ready=true. A second call or missing completion fault