n columns. scratchBytes = certificateBytes + associationHeaderBytes + associationBindingBytes, derived from validated actual schema, never a caller estimate. Header64 comprises exactly the listed six reference8 slots, extent4, index4 and lifecycleFlags8; it is an additional logical payload slot, not an object header estimate. Schema descriptors carry immutable bindings/codec metadata; captured storage references occupy the separately charged dense slice. Canonical certificate fixed84 and per-column8+V remain unchanged, including its reserved identity/owner/index slice for rejected rows; admitted identity and payload retain their original pending-snapshot byte credit. Reserve the full scratchBytes per request before eligibility, including Rejected requests with no completed certificate, and retain it throughout the reducer round. Preflight and completion check the retained per-request slice, do not spend or release scratch as transient write credit. Q-based startup reservation bounds simultaneous slices; whole-round release is Runtime-owned. No extra per-request scalar snapshot array is hidden behind the canonical bytes. Runtime framing is bounded separately as specified by operationPlan.scratchStorage.\",\"associationHeaderBytes\":64,\"associationBindingReferenceBytes\":8,\"associationHeaderLayout\":[[\"StorageReference\",8],[\"RecordIdentityReference\",8],[\"GenerationStorageTokenReference\",8],[\"FrozenSchemaReference\",8],[\"AdmittedSnapshotReference\",8],[\"SliceOwnerReference\",8],[\"CapturedExtent\",4],[\"Index\",4],[\"LifecycleFlags\",8]]}},\"admissionPrecedence\":[\"unavailable_context\",\"late_admission\",\"default_handle\",\"wrong_world\",\"retired_handle\",\"stale_generation\",\"unknown_type\",\"payload-validation-field-id-order\",\"timing-validation-duration-then-period-then-end\",\"pending_count_full\",\"control_count_full\",\"pending_bytes_full\",\"identity_exhausted\",\"generation_exhausted\",\"initial_result_full\"],\"admissionValidationOrder\":{\"pa